They definitely took one hell
of a challenge, didn't we?

40
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:54,417
Bumping her off might
have to take a back seat

41
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,577
while we figure out how
we're gonna blow this joint.

42
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,248
Don't be like that, Veggie!

43
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,457
We agreed to help Nami and her friends
escape, and that's what we'll do!

44
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:06,893
It's too late to wimp out now
just to save our own hides!

45
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,840
This is how you properly pay back a debt!

46
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:16,880
Take it easy.

47
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:18,906
Believe in the cake's flavor.

48
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:22,060
Blackleg did an extraordinary job on it.

49
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,780
Damn it, Chiffon.

50
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,019
That's what I love about you, baby.

51
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:34,440
I can see my cake!

52
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:38,160
Let's ditch these rules.

53
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,746
I hope you're ready for this.

54
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,040
You're good-for-nothing pirates!

55
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:15,860
There's another ship gaining on us!

56
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:18,159
It's Sweet General Smoothie's ship!

57
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:23,131
Big Mom may have left, but this
is still quite troublesome.

58
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,210
Careful!

59
00:04:24,293 --> 00:04:25,882
That's the weird squeezing lady!

60
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,409
Smoothie, you're here too?

61
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,847
How long will it take
to get to Kaku Island?

62
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:35,220
We're still about three hours out!

63
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,871
We should be arriving there at
1am, exactly as we promised!

64
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,860
Yeah, but we have one major problem.

65
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:45,137
We don't know when or where
Luffy is going to pop up,

66
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:48,161
and we can't warn him of
the danger ahead of time.

67
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:54,320
I believe I have a plan that could work.

68
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,559
It should get us through this mess.

69
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:08,730
Oven, sir.

70
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,137
There are more and more
ships surrounding the area.

71
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,140
Are we sure this is necessary?

72
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:14,637
It's just...

73
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:18,737
I can't really see General Katakuri
letting Straw Hat walk away, you know?

74
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:19,650
Shut up.

75
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:21,640
I'm just doing what Montour told me.

76
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:22,960
We need every unit.

77
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,137
Just trust me, okay?

78
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:25,660
Did you hear this crap?

79
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:30,417
It turns out that big explosion on the
Shit was a setup from the Straw Hats, too.

80
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,330
You're joking.

81
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,837
They may not look like
much, but at this point,

82
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:36,097
it would be a mistake if
we underestimated them.

83
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:39,004
If we let them escape,
we'll never live it down!

84
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,712
All right, I understand.

85
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,494
We will ensure their journey ends here.

86
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,220
Listen up!

87
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:48,237
In approximately three hours at 1 a .m.,

88
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:51,237
the stragglers of the Straw
Hat crew plan to meet up here.

89
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:53,757
They will try to reunite
with their captain.

90
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,857
Think of this as the last
chance to have our revenge.

91
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:59,140
To not hold back. Sir!

92
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:03,317
If by some chance Straw
Hat does manage to survive,

93
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:07,097
he's going to emerge from a mirror
located somewhere on the island.

94
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:11,533
So I need you to go into your homes
and break every single mirror in town.

95
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:15,880
Don't question my orders, just do it.

96
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,677
But sir, some of them
are family heirlooms.

97
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,297
We can't take him too lightly.

98
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,380
If you wish to spare a few,
sink them in the ocean.

99
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,140
We can salvage them later.

100
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,060
My point is simple.

101
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:32,167
This should be the only unbroken
mirror on this entire island.

102
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,340
And absolutely no exceptions.

103
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:40,840
Don't try me!

104
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,877
Should I find out that anyone here allowed

105
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:46,377
Straw Hat to escape from their own mirror,

106
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,520
your whole family will be executed.

107
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,140
Now go!

108
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:52,420
Yasuie, sir!

109
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:59,600
We'll be waiting for you,
Straw Hat. That's right.

110
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:04,420
I'm looking forward to when you
learn that this is no ordinary exit.

111
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:06,920
This is your entrance to hell.

112
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:24,257
My apologies, I failed to
notice her needles at first.

113
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,797
That was quite foolish of me. Don't worry.

114
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:30,497
About fairness, this is
a fight between pirates.

115
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:35,880
It's all my fault for not
being able to dodge them.

116
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,140
For the record,

117
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:09,097
I no longer think that you're
inferior to me really all right,

118
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,940
thanks. I guess.

119
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:21,397
Dodge me 100 times.

120
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:24,560
Failing this routine will
mean no dinner for you!

121
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:27,900
Sounds awful, right? Then focus.

122
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,470
Gotcha!

123
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,989
Thinking your opponent would
attack from the front is naive.

124
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:45,257
You'll find reading an
animal's mind is easy,

125
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:47,811
as they show their emotions on their face.

126
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:51,057
However, interpreting a
human is vastly different.

127
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:54,600
We can deceive others
and defy expectations.

128
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,150
Ouch!

129
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,040
F-f-fair!

130
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,160
I'm hungry!

131
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,717
You're a fool if you
think an enemy would stop

132
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:18,506
attacking just because
you need a lunch break.

133
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:23,880
There's intent behind
every attack by him, too.

134
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,600
I smell something delicious.

135
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:33,560
Don't pay that any mind.

136
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,060
Just my dinner.

137
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,080
Gotcha!

138
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,320
Over there!

139
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,720
You can't go attacking
your foe blindly, Luffy.

140
00:10:01,380 --> 00:10:02,860
That hurt, Rayleigh.

141
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,277
I get it, I get it.

142
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,654
I can feel your anger.

143
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,937
That's a part of Haki too.

144
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,196
Sharpen your senses.

145
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,300
You must feel your enemy's presence.

146
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,360
I said I feel your anger!

147
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,460
I'm hungry.

148
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,720
Someone there?

149
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,620
Get lost, you guys.

150
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,600
I can't take food from you.

151
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:43,419
Well, Fraley says I don't
get to eat, and no dinner.

152
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:48,020
Come on, Lucy. Focus.

153
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:00,980
It's interesting.

154
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:03,677
Your observation hockey's a bit peculiar.

155
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:08,017
It appears to be attuned to the emotions
of not only people, but animals, too.

156
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,660
Though it's unconscious, I'm sure.

157
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:13,700
Is that bad? Of course not.

158
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,529
It's quite a useful skill.

159
00:11:15,820 --> 00:11:20,585
Having that ability means you can sense
the next actions your opponent will take.

160
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,800
Make sure to practice this talent.

161
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,237
Those who master it can even
glimpse into the future.

162
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,150
That's crazy!

163
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:33,977
What are you going to do if you
come across someone like that?

164
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:35,537
Think you can take them on?

165
00:11:35,620 --> 00:11:38,561
Just two years of training
won't cut it, you know.

166
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:40,040
It'll be tough.

167
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:44,231
It'll kind of depend on what they're like.

168
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,110
Hmm?

169
00:11:46,193 --> 00:11:47,023
Their personality?

170
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,640
Why's that matter?

171
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:51,260
I've never thought of it that way.

172
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,640
Why wouldn't you?

173
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,387
You're quite the odd fellow.

174
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,540
I mean, think.

175
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:00,740
That's what it might come down to.

176
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:06,135
You're going to have some
tough times, without a doubt.

177
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:14,419
With that in mind, we can't
afford to rest for long.

178
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,140
I'll get the next lesson underway.

179
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,470
Come on.

180
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,550
Yeah!

181
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:28,280
I'm going to teach you everything
I can before your stay is up.

182
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:46,936
I'm so glad to see you.

183
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,002
Oh, that's all.

184
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,350
Oh, my God.

185
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,740
Burning mochi!

186
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:46,880
Oh, my God.

187
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:22,430
Ah!

188
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,713
If she catches up, we're toast a little.

189
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:53,500
Nah, we're good.

190
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,297
Don't forget who has the cake.

191
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:57,440
They wouldn't dare touch us.

192
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,840
Besides, at that size, Prometheus
ain't quite as nimble no more.

193
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:05,809
We'll reach La Karoo Island, so
don't you sweat at one thing.

194
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:12,812
Thanks to the quick patch-up job on
our paddles, we're back to hauling ass.

195
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:15,780
You done excellent work, fellas. Thanks!

196
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,360
That's awfully kind!

197
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:21,697
So we'll launch Land the cake onto the
island and make a break for it, right?

198
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:23,400
Yup, that's the plan.

199
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,600
Hold up, not yet.

200
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,980
What's the matter?

201
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,060
LaCour Island is too close.

202
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,957
I think we should lure her
to Fluffy Island instead.

203
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,017
What kind of harebrained idea is that?

204
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,400
Listen, Mama's having hunger pangs now.

205
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:40,417
But what do you think will happen
after she has a fill of cake?

206
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,737
She's going to come to her senses as what?

207
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:45,977
We have to give Nami more distance
or she'll go right for them.

208
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:47,317
What's so wrong with that?

209
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,997
We gotta put ourselves first.

210
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:51,517
We're gonna belly up
if we get sloppy here.

211
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:52,430
You see that?

212
00:15:52,513 --> 00:15:54,900
Mama's a monster, even more than usual.

213
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,040
My cake!

214
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:21,460
I'm dying to get a bite.

215
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:27,300
There you are.

216
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:29,700
My precious care.

217
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:33,040
We'll be together at last.

218
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:36,581
Now that you get what I'm saying?

219
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:37,530
Uh-huh.

220
00:16:37,613 --> 00:16:39,439
We're still going to Fluffy Island.

221
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:41,277
Weren't you listening to me?

222
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,900
I must pay back my debt to the Straw Hats.

223
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,180
Even if it will cost me my own life.

224
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,220
I've already made up my mind.

225
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,860
I'll go by myself if I have to.

226
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:56,937
There's been a change of plans.

227
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:59,000
To Fluffy Island on a double!

228
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,877
That's the reason you're my gal, Siobhan.

229
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:06,220
You always outdoes yourself, baby.

230
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,697
All right, let's get a move on it, boys.

231
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:14,457
Okay, if you say so far, we'll do it.

232
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:15,797
Be right back!

233
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,060
Be careful, okay, Sanji?

234
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:22,000
Will do You better not inch
any closer, you hear me, Sanji?

235
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:25,900
Keep sharp and don't drop your guard.

236
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:28,580
Take care of the Sonny, okay? Roger.

237
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:29,970
All right, Pudding.

238
00:17:30,053 --> 00:17:31,197
Let's head to the island.

239
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,868
Don't you dare pull
that crap on me, mister.

240
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:37,237
How could you lure me around
like some kind of bossy husband?

241
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:38,150
Sonny!

242
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,270
Huh?

243
00:17:41,353 --> 00:17:42,183
What was that?

244
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,510
Carrot.

245
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:45,013
Feeling better already?

246
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,020
I'm sorry, everyone.

247
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:49,319
I didn't mean to sleep for so long.

248
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:50,937
No need to apologize.

249
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:53,540
Guys, you made your Cho-Bro proud.

250
00:17:55,260 --> 00:18:00,100
During a full moon, do Cat Viper and
Dogstorm do that cool transformation too?

251
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:02,960
All Minks can do it.

252
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:06,237
If you thought I was impressive,
wait till you see them.

253
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,555
They're way stronger.

254
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:08,690
Whoa.

255
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:24,517
Touch the enemy and let me know which
direction they're attacking from!

256
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:25,920
On it! No!

257
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:27,390
Hurry!

258
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,920
I need more liquid than that.

259
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:47,837
Don't you think you're going a little far?

260
